# Database

- PostgreSQL 18 is the baseline. PostgreSQL 19 is lab-only until a frozen decision changes that.
- Flyway is append-only. Never edit an already-applied migration; add a forward migration.
- Preserve one-writer-per-schema at application and grant levels. Read `infra/AGENTS.md`.
- Prefer DB constraints over application-only validation for invariants that belong in the schema.
- Prove changes with Testcontainers-first tests. Shared Compose DB is not sole evidence.
- Activate the matching skills: `sepa-nexus-flyway-safe-change`, `postgres-rls-migration`, and when needed `debina-postgres-transaction-coordination` / `sepa-nexus-database-review` (explicit).
- Use Context7 for PostgreSQL 18 documentation.
- Use `postgres-debina` only for local runtime/schema facts.
- Never use MCP output as permission to alter a migration.
